invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64_addcarry.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh rsa-addcarry
reason: rsa_mont64_addcarry_mul no longer wipes the word that holds u, the
  last round's multiple of m, which a signer's secret operands make, so
  the stack below the signer keeps it. Only a gcc build for x86-64 runs
  the rows. The lane builds bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test for x86-64 with gcc
  and runs it under qemu-x86_64, where its two stacks under two secrets
  differ. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded
  rather than caught.

--- old
    ct_wipe(t, (2 * k + 1) * sizeof(addcarry_word));
    ct_wipe(u_word, sizeof u_word);
--- new
    ct_wipe(t, (2 * k + 1) * sizeof(addcarry_word));
    (void)u_word;
